WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:06.640
From your course dashboard, click the
Insights tab. This tab displays

cue-2
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.220
information about how students interact
with your content and assessments.

cue-3
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.560
Under the Content tab, you will see
student progress and proficiency levels

cue-4
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.420
organized by unit or module.

cue-5
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.560
This tells you in aggregate how far
students have progressed in a given

cue-6
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:30.680
section and their overall proficiency. You
can filter by searching unit names and

cue-7
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.620
selecting Student Progress or Student
Proficiency.

cue-8
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.840
In the Learning Objectives section, you
will find a proficiency breakdown

cue-9
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.720
organized by learning objectives. The
displayed analysis is based on the

cue-10
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:50.100
learning objectives you set. If your
course does not have learning objectives,

cue-11
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:56.890
no insights will appear. For example, this
course contains four learning objectives.

cue-12
00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:01.240
When you hover on the proficiency
progress bar, the detailed data will show

cue-13
00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:06.100
up for each objective. This breakdown
helps you understand where students are

cue-14
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:11.1000
excelling and where they might need extra
support. You can also filter by module to

cue-15
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.120
check on specific parts of your course.
Under Scored Activities and Practice

cue-16
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:22.840
Activities, you will see the assessment
data of each unit on students' average

cue-17
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:29.800
scores, attempts and progress. For both of
the activities tab, you can dig into one

cue-18
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:34.899
unit by clicking on it, and the questions
breakdown would appear right below the

cue-19
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:40.500
table. This shows you how students are
performing on each question, including

cue-20
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.750
attempts at incorrect answer patterns.

cue-21
00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:49.380
Note that anything you change here will
not be saved and updated to the course.

cue-22
00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:56.280
Under the Surveys tab, you can click into
the page to see survey results if your

cue-23
00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:01.679
course includes surveys. This is a great
place to check in on feedback or gather

cue-24
00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.260
formative insights from your students.
